M4: Bank1 data/bss/heap vs Bank2 “flash” + shared IPC
M4 linker: C:\Users\MeMyself\mayhem-firmware\firmware\chibios-portapack\os\ports\GCC\ARMCMx\LPC43xx_M4\ld\LPC43xx_M4.ld
“flash” region: org = 0x00000000, len = LD_M4_FLASH_LEN — shadow-mapped to Bank2 (code/rodata for the baseband image).
“ram” region: 0x10000000, len = LD_M4_RAM_LEN — Local SRAM bank 1: stacks, .data, .bss, heap from _end to __ram_end__ (full remainder of that bank).
USB bulk RAM (separate M4 memory block): ram_usb at 0x20008000, length LD_USB_RAM_LEN.
CMake sizes (same file rules.cmake):

HackRF One (non-PRALINE): M4_RAM_SIZE 96k, M4_FLASH_SIZE 32752, USB_RAM_SIZE 32k.
PRALINE: M4_RAM_SIZE 128k, M4_FLASH_SIZE 72k, USB_RAM_SIZE 32k.
Important: memory_map.hpp does not branch on PRALINE — local_sram_1 is always 40 KiB and the 26 KiB + 14 KiB split is fixed in source for shared_memory addressing. The linker’s LD_M4_FLASH_LEN can exceed 26 KiB (e.g. 32752 or 72k). There is no linker-side guarantee in the snippets you have that the executed/loaded M4 image stops before shared_memory.base(); that is a discipline / release-process invariant.

