Likely footguns
Bank2 semantic mismatch: **memory_map.hpp fixes IPC at byte 26 KiB from 0x10080000, but CMake allows LD_M4_FLASH_LEN of 32752 or 72k. If a built or decompressed baseband exceeds 26 KiB before shared_memory.base(), you corrupt IPC in RAM — not caught by static_assert (that only caps sizeof(SharedMemory), not overlap with .text/.rodata).
LZ4 decompress has no enforced output bound tied to m4_code size in m4_init — oversized SPI chunk → silent overwrite past intended code region.
Prepared .ppma M4 payloads are hard-capped at 26 KiB in the loader (ui_external_items_menu_loader.cpp), while linker may still produce larger raw M4 ELF for SPI — two different limits; easy to ship an SPI image that cannot be embedded in .ppma or vice versa.
M0 AHB is tight: 64 KiB model with 5 KB main stack + 1 KB process stack (see LPC43xx_M0.ld) + global .bss + heap until end−10 KiB + Meteor deint + G4 heap allocs + fragmentation → enable-time chHeapAlloc failures look like “random” Meteor/G4 failures.
IPC pointer rules: MeteorLrptIpc buffers must live in M0-visible AHB — if someone moved them to local SRAM or wrong region, M4 cannot see them reliably (comment in portapack_shared_memory.hpp).
rules.cmake comments vs hardware: HackRF One line says AHB 32+16 KiB split but still sets M0_RAM_SIZE “64k” — treat 64 KiB M0 RAM as the project’s chosen link map, not a guaranteed hardware maximum, if you are debugging platform mismatches.
G4 live path: single-slot ring — bursty M4 posts drop (live_ring_overflows, G4_DROP_RING_OVERFLOW) if M0 worker is slow; not RAM exhaustion but looks like “missing frames”.
Recommended stable allocation strategy
Treat memory_map.hpp as the hard contract for Bank2: keep M4 executable footprint (loaded or decompressed) ≤ m4_code.size() (26 KiB) ending strictly before shared_memory.base(); treat LD_M4_FLASH_LEN as an upper linker ceiling, not permission to grow into IPC unless you change memory_map + both cores’ agreement.
Guarantee SPI image size: add release checks (map file / CI) that .text+.rodata (and LZ4 decompress output) for image_tag_meteor_lrpt_rx stay under 26 KiB (or lift both map + loader + flash layout together).
M0: prefer static budgets for always-on Meteor structures; keep large, optional paths heap-backed at enable (as deint/G4 already do) and fail loudly in UI when ensure_deint_buffers() / chHeapAlloc fails — avoid silent magic = 0 regressions during bring-up.
M4: assume Bank1 pressure — the two 16 KiB soft .bss blocks dominate; before adding buffers, inspect MAP totals; interleaved_post_ intentionally delayed — keep expensive allocs lazy until mode is confirmed.
External packaging: enforce consistent maximum_application_size, .ppma M4 slice ≤ 26 KiB, and metadata (external_app_info.py + export_external_apps.py) whenever Meteor blob size changes — avoid shipping SPI-only blobs that exceed .ppma limits.
